  "about": "The tractus of the formulary “First Sunday of Lent” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "He that dwelleth in the aid of the Most High shall abide under the protection of the God of heaven. He shall say unto the Lord: Thou art my defender and my refuge; He is my God, in Him will I hope. For He hath delivered me from the snare of the hunters and from the sharp word. With His shoulders He shall overshadow thee, and under His wings shalt thou trust. His truth shall compass thee with a shield; thou shalt not fear the terror of the night, the arrow that flieth by day, the evil that walketh about in darkness, ruin, or the noonday demon. A thousand shall fall at thy side and ten thousand at thy right hand, but it shall not come nigh thee. For He hath given His angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways. In their hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone. Thou shalt walk upon the asp and the basilisk, and thou shalt trample the lion and the dragon under foot. Because he hath hoped in Me, I will deliver him; I will protect him, because he hath known My name. He shall call upon Me, and I will hear him; I am with him in tribulation. I will deliver him and glorify him; with length of days I will fill him and show him My salvation." }
  },
